'' T48, RUN: a constructor that writes 'base( ... )' keeps its own vtable. Its prologue
'' -- fields, then the vptr -- used to be emitted in front of the body, so the base
'' constructor's vptr store came last and won: a Square built through 'base( s, s )'
'' answered 'rect' through a Rect ptr. And the fields were constructed before the base.
'' Output identical to fbc-modern's for the same program.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/base-call-vptr.bas -o tests/codegen/basecallvptr.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/basecallvptr.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/basecallvptr.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: Base1 constructor, Who() = Base1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: Part (a field) constructed
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: Der1 body, Who() = Der1, n = 7, k = 42
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: through Base1: Der1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: through Rect: square cube 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: new through Rect: cube
